  "holistic_F_N": 0,
  "holistic_F_H": 0,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires 24-hour regulator reporting for all thermal incidents, written reports within 10 days, and 72-hour customer notices for credible risks. S2 sets a 55°C test with a 5% permanent failure cap, immediate sales stop for failing models, and numeric per-model rates to customers but not the public. S3 mandates new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit window; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8 incidents/100k with prompt notices and no phase-in."
 },
